%
% Probabilistic marginal under a declared independence model (#506 AC-1).
% rain and sprinkler are independent Bernoulli facts (p=0.5 each); a noisy-OR
% rule makes the ground wet whenever either holds. Under logic:FullIndependence:
%   P(wet) = 1 - (1-0.5)(1-0.5) = 0.75.
% Expected: X = ex:yes with probability 0.75, status ok.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-marginal-independent/').
:- probability_model(full_independence).
:- probability(ex:rain(ex:today, ex:yes), 0.5).
:- probability(ex:sprinkler(ex:today, ex:yes), 0.5).
ex:wet(D, ex:yes) :- ex:rain(D, ex:yes).
ex:wet(D, ex:yes) :- ex:sprinkler(D, ex:yes).
?- ex:wet(ex:today, X).
